-- title:
--   Formally smooth centred chart subalgebra at a non-supersingular centre (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Fix the prime $q$ with $q = 2$ and a level $M'$ with $M' \neq 0$ and $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ — the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by $j_q$ and its level-$M'$ expansion — such that, by `hW`, $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. those places that are rational, affine-geometric, and whose value at the geometric $j$-invariant lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$. Let `hle` be the inclusion of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with unit group $H = \ker(\mathrm{unitsMap})$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the compatibility axioms of that structure; the hypothesis `hR₀` requires that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and that its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, and let $\zeta$ be an element of $\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which says that $f$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ precisely when there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ after pushing $x,y$ into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which says that every $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is permuted by taking preimages along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$. The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s$ the constants in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ are exactly the elements of $A$; `hSS_over`, that for each $s \in W$ and each $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is non-negative at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which the order of the modular invariant $j_q$ is non-negative and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ under `hle` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that for each $s$ there is $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The descent data are: a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation ring $A_0$ (a commutative domain) together with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`) and such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`); a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`hϖ₀π`); a subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; the hypothesis `hjF₀` that the element $\hat\jmath$, the image under `hle` of $j_q$ viewed in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, lies in $F_0$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map agrees with $\iota$ followed by $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (`hj₀`); and the assumption $\hat\jmath \neq 0$ in $F_0$.
--
--   Finally, let $V$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ with: `hV`, every element of $V$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$; `hVlt`, some element of $F_0$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ but not in $V$, so the inclusion is strict; and `hCV`, the chart algebra $C = \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$, consisting of the elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$, is contained in $V$. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ which by `h𝔫` consists exactly of those $g \in C$ whose image in $F_0$ is a non-unit of $V$, so $\mathfrak n$ is the centre of $V$ on $C$. The hypothesis `hnotSS` states that for every $s \in W$ some $g \in C$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ but not in $\mathfrak n$. A family $\mathfrak q$ of ideals of $C$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ is given with: `hLOC`, for each $\ell$ the elements of $F_0$ lying in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ are exactly the fractions $b/c$ with $b, c \in C$ and $c \notin \mathfrak q(\ell)$; `hMIN`, each $\mathfrak q(\ell)$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; `hINJ`, injectivity of $\mathfrak q$; and `hSURJ`, every minimal prime over that ideal is some $\mathfrak q(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hGENFIB` states that for every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ not containing the image of $\varpi_0$ there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ whose elements are exactly the fractions $b/c$ with $b, c \in C$ and $c \notin \mathfrak p$. Lastly, $U$ is an open subscheme of the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$ (the pushout of the two maps from the spectrum of the middle chart algebra to the spectra of the finite and infinite chart algebras), the image of the prime $\mathfrak n$ under the base map of $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ lies in $U$ (`hxU`), and the open immersion $U \to \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}$ followed by the structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ is smooth (`hU`).
--
--   Under these assumptions there exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$ such that all of the following hold. (i) $B$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra. (ii) $B$ is integrally closed in $F_0$: every $x \in F_0$ integral over $B$ lies in $B$. (iii) $F_0$ is the fraction field of $B$: every $x \in F_0$ can be written as $x = b/c$ with $b, c \in B$, $c \neq 0$. (iv) Every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ which contains the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and is not maximal is a minimal prime over that ideal. (v) For every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ not containing that ideal there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ whose elements are exactly the $f \in F_0$ of the form $f = b/c$ with $b, c \in B$ and $c \notin \mathfrak p$. (vi) The only $\ell' \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell')$ containing the image of all of $B$ is $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$. (vii) For no $s \in W$ does $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contain the image of all of $B$. (viii) There is a prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ such that an element $x \in F_0$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ if and only if $x = b/c$ with $b, c \in B$ and $c \notin \mathfrak q$. (ix) The same localisation description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ holds for every minimal prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ over the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$. (x) $B \subseteq V$. (xi) $\mathfrak m$ consists exactly of those $b \in B$ whose image in $F_0$ is a non-unit of $V$. (xii) Either $\hat\jmath \in B$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1} \in B$. (xiii) The structure map from $A_0$ to the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$ is formally smooth.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the chart step in the Igusa-chart dichotomy for semistable coverings of modular curves with full level structure: starting from a strict valuation-theoretic refinement $V$ of the Igusa ring at $\infty$ whose centre on the $\hat\jmath$-finite chart is maximal, is not a supersingular centre, and has a neighbourhood smooth over the descended base $A_0$, it produces a finitely generated, integrally closed, suitably centred chart algebra $B$ with formally smooth localisation at its centre. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent_of_eq_two), which combines it with the alternative branch of the dichotomy.
